<DocsLayout
  title="Wallets — Overview"
  description="Universal credential wallet discovery layer. Solves the NASCAR problem with CustomEvent-based discovery, zero runtime dependencies, and 4 wire protocols."
  currentPath="/docs/wallets/"
>
  <h1>Wallets</h1>
  <p class="docs-hero-sub">
    <code>@attestto/id-wallet-adapter</code> v0.4.1
  </p>

  <p>
    Universal discovery layer for credential wallet browser extensions. Instead
    of hard-coding support for each wallet, your application announces what it
    needs and wallets respond if they can fulfill the request.
  </p>

  <h2>The NASCAR Problem</h2>
  <p>
    Every relying party shouldn't need a grid of wallet logos. The adapter uses a
    <strong>CustomEvent-based discovery protocol</strong> — no server required.
    Wallets announce themselves; your app picks the best match.
  </p>

  <h2>Key Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Zero runtime dependencies</strong> — ships as a single ESM module</li>
    <li><strong>CustomEvent discovery</strong> — wallets announce via <code>wallet-announce</code> events, no polling</li>
    <li><strong>4 wire protocols</strong> — CHAPI, OID4VP, DIDComm v2, WACI-DIDComm</li>
    <li><strong>Built-in picker modal</strong> — or bring your own UI</li>
    <li><strong>QR fallback</strong> — reaches mobile wallets when no extension is installed</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Quick Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash">
    <Fragment set:html={`npm install @attestto/id-wallet-adapter`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript">
    <Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> { pickWallet } <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto/id-wallet-adapter'</span>

<span class="c-kw">const</span> wallet = <span class="c-kw">await</span> <span class="c-fn">pickWallet</span><span class="c-br">(</span><span class="c-br">{</span>
  <span class="c-attr">requiredProtocols</span>: <span class="c-br">[</span><span class="c-str">'oid4vp'</span><span class="c-br">]</span>,
  <span class="c-attr">requiredGoals</span>: <span class="c-br">[</span><span class="c-str">'authentication'</span><span class="c-br">]</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span><span class="c-br">)</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

